    "body": "Pronunciation and wording lessons from the DeepSeek V4.1 overview video (2026-10-18), most of them from the user's review.\n\n- **GiB / KiB** (user's ear): read like GB / KB. New lexicon entries `GiB → G B`, `KiB → K B`. Before, the voice garbled them (Whisper heard GIG / TB); a letter-by-letter G I B reading was tried and rejected by the user.\n- **MoE** (user's ear): read as \"Mo\", like the name *Moe*. New lexicon entries `MoE` / `DeepSeekMoE` / `MegaMoE` → `M O E`; the `moe` part (identifiers like `fused_moe`) now maps to `M O E`; MoE is removed from the \"reads right as written\" list.\n- **key** (as in \"indexer key\"): heard as T in every carrier, including 索引 key. Added to the reword table; narration says 索引键 / 键 and the term stays on screen.\n- **Chinese polyphones across a word boundary** (user's ear): 「生成长距离」 was read as 生成 zhǎng 距离, because the voice formed 「成长」 across the boundary. 「decoder 侧重放」 was read as 侧重 (cè zhòng). `pron_check` cannot see these because Whisper writes the same character for either reading. Added a note to `references/pronunciation.md`: scan for polyphones whose neighbour forms another word before TTS, reword (「侧的重放」), and prefer dictionary words (重新算 over 重算).\n- **Glossary compliance** (user review): a title said 预填. `references/house-style.md` now says to grep the narration and the on-screen strings for Chinese renderings of glossary terms (预填 → prefill, 前缀 → prefix, 每批 / 批次 → batch, 内核, 混批) before TTS.\n\nChecks:\n- `pron_check --script` reports 0 issues after the changes.\n- `to_spoken` gives `Deep Seek M O E` / `M O E` / `fused M O E`.\n- The video was re-voiced and re-rendered with these fixes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
