      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/BBuf/AI-Infra-Auto-Driven-SKILLS/contents/skills%2Fsglang-explainer-video%2Freferences%2Fhouse-style.md?ref=c35daca24c628e2846a90b2cef0b8241a3b372f6",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "skills/sglang-explainer-video/references/house-style.md",
      "patch": "@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@ Every rule here came from a correction on a delivered video. Apply all of them b\n   kernel (never 内核), batch / mixed batch / mixed chunk (never 混批), prefill, decode, decode tail, prefix,\n   token, attention, metadata, output buffer, fallback, bit-exact, micro benchmark, profile, launch, step, CFG,\n   GEMM, quant, epilogue, branch, review, PR. Everyday words stay Chinese: 吞吐, 耗时, 并发, 端到端.\n+  Grep the narration **and the on-screen Scene strings** for Chinese renderings before TTS — 预填 (→ prefill),\n+  前缀 (→ prefix), 每批 / 批次 (→ batch), 内核, 混批 — the user flagged 预填 on a title (DeepSeek V4.1 video, 2026-10-18).\n - Write numbers as digits (15%, 3.79 ms); the TTS reads them correctly and captions show them verbatim.\n - **Completeness over brevity.** No time limit: the film is as long as it takes to explain every algorithm\n   and code detail of the PR / article so a viewer can follow it. Pace per frame, not per film: one idea per",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/BBuf/AI-Infra-Auto-Driven-SKILLS/raw/c35daca24c628e2846a90b2cef0b8241a3b372f6/skills%2Fsglang-explainer-video%2Freferences%2Fhouse-style.md",
      "sha": "112b22f7643220714b0fd42122decf67ca536ef0",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 12,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/BBuf/AI-Infra-Auto-Driven-SKILLS/blob/c35daca24c628e2846a90b2cef0b8241a3b372f6/skills%2Fsglang-explainer-video%2Freferences%2Fpronunciation.md",
      "changes": 13,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/BBuf/AI-Infra-Auto-Driven-SKILLS/contents/skills%2Fsglang-explainer-video%2Freferences%2Fpronunciation.md?ref=c35daca24c628e2846a90b2cef0b8241a3b372f6",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "skills/sglang-explainer-video/references/pronunciation.md",
      "patch": "@@ -66,10 +66,12 @@ voice changes.\n | LoRA | Lora | Lauren → **Laura** |\n | Miles | mials | Mouse → **Miles** |\n | AIME (AIME25, AIME 2025) | Aime | M → **AIM** (short sentence; in a long line Whisper still writes M — read as \"aim\", the usual reading) |\n+| GiB / KiB (binary units) | G B / K B | **user's ear, 2026-10-18**: say them like GB / KB, not letter by letter (G I B was rejected). Whisper hears GB / KB, so `pron_check` reports KiB as a FAIL against the written form; that is expected |\n+| **MoE** (also DeepSeekMoE, MegaMoE, fused_moe) | M O E (lexicon + `parts`) | **user's ear, 2026-10-18**: the voice said \"Mo\" (the English name *Moe*). Spelled letters come back as MOE |\n | VAE / DiT / GEMM | V A E / D I T / G E M M | V / Date / (dropped) → **VAE / DIT / GEMM** |\n | DRAFT_EXTEND_V2 | draft extend V two | Draft下划线Extend下划线V2 → **Draft Extend V2** |\n \n-These read right as written: PR, DSA, MLA, MTP, MoE, KV cache, fused, prefill, decode, batch, token,\n+These read right as written: PR, DSA, MLA, MTP, KV cache, fused, prefill, decode, batch, token,\n kernel, attention, indexer, backend, CUDA graph, FP8/FP4/NVFP4, TP8, H200/B200/GB300, Triton, PyTorch,\n torch.compile, vLLM, NVIDIA, Blackwell, Hopper, RoPE, RMSNorm, softmax, Mamba, Ulysses, GLM-5.3, W4AFP8.\n \n@@ -91,9 +93,18 @@ worse), Lean (\"Lin\"), README (\"Remi\"), TopK (\"Talk K\"), FLUX.2 (fine in most sen\n | ncu | 看 | Nsight Compute (passes: N-Sight Compute) |\n | swizzle | Swizo | 交错排列的内存布局 |\n | scatter (Beam video, 2026-10-17) | Statter | 「先 gather，算完再分发回去」 |\n+| key (indexer key, DSV4.1 video 2026-10-18) | T (in every carrier, also 索引 key) | 索引键 / 读键的带宽 |\n \n Also OK~ in that video, listen on the render: warp / warps (\"World\" / \"Works\"), grid (\"Grip\"), tile (\"他\").\n \n+**Chinese polyphones across a word boundary** (user's ear, DeepSeek V4.1 video 2026-10-18): 「生成长距离」 was read\n+「生成 zhǎng 距离」 because the voice segmented the bigram 「成长」 (chéng zhǎng) across the word boundary. `pron_check` cannot\n+catch this: Whisper writes 长 for either reading. Before TTS, scan the narration for a polyphone (长 / 行 / 重 / 还 / 得 /\n+了 / 差 / 便 …) whose neighbour forms a different word (成长, 生长, 银行, 重复 …) and reword so the bigram never forms,\n+e.g. 「40 层里只有 4 层在生成长距离 KV」 → 「40 层里，长距离 KV 只由 4 层生成」.\n+Same review: 「decoder 侧重放」 was read cè**zhòng** fàng (侧重 = emphasis) → 「decoder 侧的重放」. Also prefer the dictionary\n+word over a clipped one: 「重算」 is not a common word and may get zhòng, so write 「重新算」.\n+\n In-context checks of long lines are noisy: re-probe a FAIL in a short sentence before changing the lexicon. In\n the 13-video re-voice, most FAILs read right in the short sentence. If one sounds wrong, reword the line, e.g. \"EAGLE 投机解码\" → \"投机解码（EAGLE）\" on\n screen only.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/BBuf/AI-Infra-Auto-Driven-SKILLS/raw/c35daca24c628e2846a90b2cef0b8241a3b372f6/skills%2Fsglang-explainer-video%2Freferences%2Fpronunciation.md",
